            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sanzoe"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was so much better than I thought it would be. The flavors meld well together but not overpowering. I served with warm pretzels. This would be fabulous on vegetables, chicken, steak, really anything."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Joseph Ferris"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This butter is a staple with our Christmas dinner, served with fresh pretzel rolls. The only thing that I have changed is that I have replaced the Dijon mustard with stone ground mustard, which provides a more distinct flavor. I have to normally quadruple the recipe, due to how popular it is. If anyone feels turned off by the anchovy paste, don't be! It provides a deep umami with absolutely no fish flavor.",
            "datePublished": "2017-12-17T23:21:38.070Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sandra G"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I liked it very much. I had a very refined anchovy paste - I think I could have used a bit more. Same with the Worcestershire sauce. On the other hand, the mustard was a little too evident. I made too much for one person, but I put the leftover into an ice cube container and deep froze it for the next piece of meat.",
            "datePublished": "2012-09-23T11:51:03.717Z"
          },
